# Security & Performance Rules

## Security Guidelines

### HTTPS & Mixed Content
- **HTTPS Only**: All external resources (scripts, stylesheets, images) must use HTTPS
- **Mixed Content Prevention**: Never load HTTP resources on HTTPS pages
- **Protocol Relative URLs**: Use // instead of http:// or https:// when appropriate
- **CDN Security**: Use trusted CDNs with HTTPS support

### Input Validation & Sanitization
- **User Input Validation**: Validate all user inputs before processing
- **XSS Prevention**: Sanitize data before rendering in HTML templates
- **SQL Injection Prevention**: Use parameterized queries and input validation
- **File Upload Security**: Validate file types, sizes, and scan for malware

### API Security
- **Token Management**: Never expose sensitive tokens in client-side code
- **Environment Variables**: Store API keys and secrets in environment variables
- **CORS Configuration**: Properly configure CORS headers for API endpoints
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse

### Data Protection
- **Sensitive Data**: Never log or display sensitive information (passwords, tokens, PII)
- **Data Encryption**: Encrypt sensitive data in transit and at rest
- **Session Management**: Use secure session handling and proper logout
- **Access Control**: Implement proper access controls and authentication

## Performance Optimization

### Resource Loading
- **CDN Usage**: Load all external libraries from reliable CDNs
- **Minification**: Use minified versions of libraries in production
- **Compression**: Enable gzip/brotli compression for text-based assets
- **Caching Headers**: Set appropriate cache headers for static assets

### JavaScript Performance
- **Lazy Loading**: Load components and modules only when needed
- **Event Delegation**: Use event delegation for dynamic content
- **Memory Management**: Clean up event listeners, timers, and chart instances
- **Debouncing/Throttling**: Implement debouncing for frequent events (resize, scroll)

### CSS Performance
- **Critical CSS**: Inline critical CSS for above-the-fold content
- **CSS Optimization**: Remove unused CSS and minimize specificity conflicts
- **Animation Performance**: Use transform and opacity for animations
- **Media Queries**: Use efficient media queries and avoid unnecessary repaints

### Image Optimization
- **Image Formats**: Use appropriate formats (WebP, AVIF for modern browsers)
- **Responsive Images**: Use srcset and sizes attributes for responsive images
- **Lazy Loading**: Implement lazy loading for images below the fold
- **Compression**: Optimize images without losing quality

## Browser Compatibility

### Cross-Browser Support
- **Feature Detection**: Use feature detection instead of browser detection
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Ensure core functionality works without JavaScript
- **Fallback Handling**: Provide alternatives when features aren't supported
- **Testing**: Test across major browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)

### Mobile Optimization
- **Touch Targets**: Ensure touch targets are at least 44px × 44px
- **Viewport Configuration**: Use proper viewport meta tags
- **Performance**: Optimize for mobile network conditions
- **Accessibility**: Ensure mobile accessibility compliance

## Error Handling & Monitoring

### Error Management
- **Graceful Degradation**: Handle errors gracefully without breaking the UI
- **User Feedback**: Provide clear, actionable error messages
- **Error Logging**: Log errors for debugging and monitoring
- **Recovery Mechanisms**: Implement automatic retry and recovery logic

### Performance Monitoring
- **Metrics Tracking**: Monitor Core Web Vitals and performance metrics
- **Real User Monitoring**: Track actual user experience and performance
- **Alerting**: Set up alerts for performance degradation
- **Optimization**: Continuously optimize based on performance data

## Code Quality for Performance

### Efficient Algorithms
- **Time Complexity**: Choose efficient algorithms and data structures
- **Memory Usage**: Minimize memory footprint and avoid memory leaks
- **Loop Optimization**: Use efficient loops and avoid unnecessary iterations
- **Caching**: Implement appropriate caching strategies

### Bundle Optimization
- **Tree Shaking**: Remove unused code from bundles
- **Code Splitting**: Split code into smaller, loadable chunks
- **Dependency Management**: Keep dependencies up to date and minimal
- **Bundle Analysis**: Regularly analyze bundle size and composition
